# Nimbus configuration: the variable names the app understands.
#
# The app reads these from environment variables. It does NOT load a .env file
# automatically. To override a default, export the variable before starting:
#   export NIMBUS_DATA_DIR=/some/folder
#   python3 -m streamlit run src/app.py
# If you keep your values in a local .env file, load it with:
#   set -a; source .env; set +a
# Never commit a real .env file: it is listed in .gitignore.
#
# With nothing set, Nimbus uses local defaults: Markdown copies of saved
# discussions in ./analyses-data/ and SQLite at ./analyses-data/nimbus.db.

# Folder for the Markdown copy of each saved discussion (the complete snapshot
# used to reopen it is stored in the database).
# On EC2 this is the instance's EBS root disk (Lesson 7 design); the
# CloudFormation template sets it to:
# NIMBUS_DATA_DIR=/home/ec2-user/nimbus/analyses-data

# Database for clients, discussions and company values (SQLAlchemy URL).
# Local development (default):
# NIMBUS_DATABASE_URL=sqlite:////absolute/path/to/nimbus.db
#
# Amazon RDS for MySQL (CloudFormation Stage 2 sets this on EC2). Use placeholders here only; supply the
# real values through CloudFormation parameters or the instance environment.
# Keep the password to letters and digits so it needs no URL encoding.
# NIMBUS_DATABASE_URL=mysql+pymysql://<username>:<password>@<rds-endpoint>:3306/<database-name>

# Time zone for displayed times and for the "Saved from / to" search dates (IANA name).
# Times are always stored in UTC. Default: Asia/Singapore.
# NIMBUS_TIMEZONE=Asia/Singapore
